### Dependencies resolved by vcpkg, not vendored

`vcpkg.json` names these; they are fetched at configure time and are not in
this repository.

- **DirectX Tool Kit for DX11** (`directxtk`) — MIT, Microsoft Corporation.
- **DirectXMath**, which `directxtk` brings — MIT, Microsoft Corporation.
- **The XAudio2 redistributable** (`xaudio2redist`, `directxtk`'s feature) —
  the Microsoft Software License Terms for it, which vcpkg installs as
  `share/xaudio2redist/copyright`.
- **doctest** — MIT, Viktor Kirilov.
- **lodepng** — zlib, Lode Vandevenne. Linked only by `RenderPixelTests`, to
  read and write its golden PNGs.

What a game built on Labrador carries to its players, and the file that
carries each notice, is the website's *Ship a Windows release* guide
(`website/src/content/docs/docs/guides/windows-release.mdx`), whose list is
`website/src/components/ReleaseNotices.astro`; the Get Started project's
install rules put those files in its release folder.

### Linked into a browser build by its toolchain

A `wasm-*` build links Emscripten's runtime and system libraries statically
into every module it makes, so they are distributed wherever a module is.
None of them is in this tree; each comes with the Emscripten install and
carries its licence there.

- **Emscripten's runtime and system libraries**, including its JavaScript
  loader and its html5 and GL implementations — MIT or University of
  Illinois/NCSA, at the recipient's choice, Emscripten authors.
- **libc++, libc++abi, libunwind and compiler-rt's builtins** — Apache License
  2.0 with LLVM Exceptions, the LLVM Project.
- **Emscripten's C library**, derived from musl — MIT, Rich Felker, et al.
- **dlmalloc** — public domain (CC0), Doug Lea.

LineSweeper's web bundle carries these notices with it: the build writes a
`NOTICE.txt` beside the module, from `samples/linesweeper/web/NOTICE.txt` and
the full licence texts in the Emscripten install that linked it. It also
includes this record and Microsoft's MIT text for the shared timer code,
preserved byte for byte as `tools/web_bundle/Microsoft-LICENSE.txt` from
https://github.com/microsoft/DirectXTK/blob/a0a1ab67d9d8f1a41b76c0950eb37f27d6bf355d/LICENSE.
The website's *Build for the browser* guide
(`website/src/content/docs/docs/guides/browser.mdx`, *Gather the browser
release and its notices*) gives the same bundling step for a copied template.

### Toolchains, not code

These tools, headers and import libraries are installed separately and are not
carried in this source tree. Builds run the tools and link the platform import
libraries named below. They are listed so that "what does this repository need
that it does not ship" has one answer.

- **The Windows 10/11 SDK** — `fxc`, for the two Direct3D backends' shader, and
  the Direct3D and DXGI headers and import libraries.
- **The Vulkan SDK** (LunarG) — for the Vulkan backend only, and it is the one
  dependency here that does not arrive with Visual Studio or with Windows. The
  build uses its `dxc` to compile `engine/render/sprite.hlsl` to SPIR-V, and
  links `vulkan-1.lib`, which is an import library for a loader that ships with
  graphics drivers. Its own components carry their own licences; none of them
  is redistributed here.

## Content

The content under `samples/` supplies the runnable examples. Original audio
in `samples/audio/source/` and its compiled `content/sounds/tones.xwb` are
generated by the accompanying script and covered by the repository's MIT
licence; the audio sample's README records the authoring tool and commands.

### Fonts

#### JetBrains Mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1)

`jetbrains_mono_bold_16.spritefont` is a glyph atlas rendered from JetBrains
Mono Bold, version 2.304. There are three copies of it, byte for byte the same,
each with the font's licence beside it as `OFL.txt`:

- `samples/minimal/content/fonts/`, which the collision, components,
  local_multiplayer and audio samples also load, and which a game copying the
  template takes with it
- `samples/linesweeper/content/fonts/`
- `tests/render/content/`

Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors
(https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono). Licensed under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1, whose full text is each `OFL.txt`. The atlas is a
Modified Version of the font in that licence's terms, so the OFL covers it
rather than Labrador's MIT licence. The licence lets it be used, embedded and
redistributed, inside a game that is sold as much as in one that is not, on
two conditions that matter here: every copy carries the copyright notice and
the licence, and the font is not sold by itself. It names no Reserved Font
Name. The font file itself is not in this repository; `samples/minimal/README.md`
says where it came from and how the atlas was built.
